                </p><pre><b>PMWATCH</b> (ATLANTA) - APRIL 19, 2002 -- For the past weeks, AJC has shown an 
unbalanced trend in its opinion page with regard to the Palestinian-Israeli 
conflict.  Tuesdays racist opinions (April 16) included Mona Charens denying 
the existence of Palestinians.  In the second Op-Ed the writer uses the Irish 
troubles as a backdrop to assailing the Palestinians.  Consistent with the 
recent trend opinions from the Palestinian side are absent.

To live to the basic standards of journalistic integrity the balance on the
opinion pages needs to be addressed immediately

Included below:
- Excerpts from the Op-Eds
- Talking Points
- The Op-Eds

Palestine Media Watch Contact:  Rani El-Hajjar, suhmati@hotmail.com

ACTION(s) REGQUESTED:

CALL, EMAIL and FAX the Public Editor Mr. Mike King, 404-526-5819, fax
404-526-5311,

(As your liaison to the newsroom, the Public Editor takes comments from our
readers about fairness and accuracy in news coverage and editorial pages)

Or use the interface below to send an email. You email will be sent to:
insideajc@ajc.com; Cc:  rmartin@ajc.com, dbeasley@ajc.com, 
bsenftleber@ajc.com, cynthia@ajc.com, rkintzel@ajc.com

EXCERPTS FROM 4/15/02 OP-EDS
http://www.creators.com/opinion_show.cfm?next=2&amp;ColumnsName=mch
http://www.accessatlanta.com/ajc/opinion/0402/0416konner.html

- Further, these Arab refugees had no ancient tie to the land of
"Palestine."

- The whole idea of a Palestinian nation and a Palestinian people is an
invention of Arab propaganda.

- It is not and never was "Palestinian land."
- At Camp David in 2000, Yasser Arafat rejected an offer of more than 90
percent of the land he wants, yet he wouldn't even negotiate from that as a
starting point, a place from which to work toward a free, coherent state.
Israel's government can in time remove many settlements; it can control its
few extremists. But Arafat can't or won't control his, and their actions
echo Sept. 11 every day.

TALKING POINTS

* Upon tracking the AJC daily the pro-Israeli bias in the opinion page is
evident, we ask that you represent the Palestinian side.

* Balance means not only "Israel-can-do-no-wrong" columnists are given all
the space.

* The Palestinian opinion should be represented clearly, as there are
Europeans, Jewish, Arab Americans.

* The NY Times, LA Times, Chicago Tribune, and other mainstream newspapers
print alternative opinion columns - when will the Atlanta Journal live up to
this diverse and multicultural cities reputation?

* If asked who suggested you call the AJC, mention Palestine Media Watch.

* In the past few months, we estimate that the number of non-pro-Israel,
non-Israeli-government line pieces to be 2.  During the same period, there
were tens of the blame-Arafat, only-Israeli-suffering-counts,
Sharon-is-doing-the-right-thing columns.

* Pro-Isreali columnists: Between them they write at least 8 REGULAR COLUMNS
PER WEEK!

William Safire
Mona Charen
George Will
Thomas Friendman
Thomas Sowell
Bill O'Reilly
and others.

* Neutral columnists: Molly Ivins

